<title>JAPAN: Nittetsu Mining sees copper output edging up.</title>
<headline>Nittetsu Mining sees copper output edging up.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nittetsu Mining Co said on Thursday its planned copper output for the first half of fiscal 1997/98 was 19,300 tonnes, up slightly from 18,900 tonnes in the first and the second half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>Its scheduled output for the first half of fiscal 1997/98, estimated output in the 1996/97 second half and actual output in the 1996/97 first half were as follows:</p>
<p>		    H1-1997/98  H2-1996/97  H1-1996/97</p>
<p>Copper (tonnes)   19,300	18,900	18,900</p>
<p>Gold (kg)		873	   934	   866</p>
<p>Silver (kg)	  2,672	 3,765	 3,651</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
